  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 18 is the longest at Ralph Williamson at 607 feet — a par 4 that plays across the water and gives the course its most memorable moment. With the Cascades or Olympics on the horizon and the hazard in play, it's the hole that makes this neighborhood park feel like a destination.",
  "localTips": "The water carry on the final hole is the round's defining moment — plan your line. Pet friendly with restrooms on site. Free to play in a multi-use park; weekday mornings are the quiet time.",
